"sharing.transfer.title" = "Data Transfer and Ongoing Updates";
"sharing.transfer.setup" = "This goes beyond a local preview. After confirmation, selected events are copied with your chosen visibility to a separate calendar in the selected account and synced by its provider. Even events stored only on this device may be uploaded. These changes take effect only after final confirmation; existing shared calendars continue updating under their confirmed rules meanwhile.";
"sharing.transfer.destination" = "After confirmation, copies are written to the account shown above and can be synced to its provider by the system. Apple handles iCloud; another provider handles other accounts. Source events stored only on this device or in another account are also copied to this account.";
"sharing.transfer.fields" = "Every shared event includes start and end times, time zone, all-day status, and availability. Availability only uses an availability placeholder title; Title & time adds the original title; Title, location & notes also includes location and notes, which may contain meeting links or personal information. Individual visibility settings take precedence; Do not share creates no copy. Attendees, organizers, alarms, attachments, and the source event URL are not copied.";
"sharing.transfer.ongoing" = "Confirmation also allows ongoing updates under the confirmed rules, including new and changed source events and rolling dates, without asking for each event. While paused, settings are saved and writes resume only after you resume updates. If sharing is enabled, people with access may receive updates. Anyone holding a public link can read the shared content and forward the link. Received copies cannot be recalled.";
"sharing.transfer.confirm" = "I agree to transfer the content above to the selected account and allow ongoing updates";
"sharing.resume.title" = "Resume Data Transfer and Updates?";
"sharing.resume.confirm" = "Confirm and Resume Updates";
"sharing.resume.message" = "Destination account: %@.\nResuming writes copies using the confirmed sources, dates, and visibility for the account provider to sync. This includes new or changed events while paused and events entering the rolling range. People with access may receive updates, without a separate prompt for each event.";
"share.calendar.link.privacy.title" = "Who Can Access a Public Link";
"share.calendar.link.privacy.help" = "Anyone with a public calendar link can read its contents and forward the link. This is an ongoing subscription, so recipients may keep receiving updates within your confirmed rules. Importing stores the link locally without checking it or enabling sharing; sending passes it to the share app you choose. Pausing updates or replacing the locally saved link does not revoke access. Disable public sharing in Apple Calendar to revoke access; copies already saved by others cannot be recalled.";

